summary:
- topic: Student Representative Recognition
  text: The Board and members of the public offered extensive praise and thanks to
    departing student representative Elliot Wertheimer for his dedicated and insightful
    service during his senior year.
- topic: Student Leadership Update
  text: The Board recognized student representative Angela on her re-election for
    a third term and welcomed incoming representative Alex Davison, who was present
    in the audience.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Referendum
  text: The Superintendent provided details on the June 10th school budget referendum
    for the FY2026 operational budget, clarifying that it is separate from any future
    bond for athletic complex improvements and explaining the process if the referendum
    fails.
- topic: Public Comment
  text: During public comment, the South Portland Teachers Association president urged
    the community to vote in favor of the budget, while other teachers and citizens
    lamented the resignations of valued colleagues.
- topic: Pre-K Special Education
  text: The Assistant Superintendent explained the district's ongoing "fact-finding"
    approach to the multi-year state-mandated transition of responsibility for pre-K
    special education services from Child Development Services (CDS) to local districts.
- topic: Personnel Approvals
  text: The Board unanimously approved several personnel elections, including the
    hiring of Abigail Chen as the new district Finance Director, who was introduced
    to the board.
